\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\title{Limitations}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The limitations are relative to the purpose in
[Motivation and aim](fnip-0020).}

\p{The notes contain the Introduction and the chapters through
the classes of excitability.
[State variables and phase space](fnip-0002) contains the Morris–Lecar
pair, the trajectory, and one voltage trace.
[[fnip-0026]] is, in what is written, local existence and uniqueness
for a continuously differentiable velocity, the linearization at
an equilibrium, and, near a hyperbolic equilibrium, a homeomorphism
onto the linear orbits together with the
[local stable and unstable manifolds](fnip-0044), and a
[closed orbit](fnip-0052) of the planar Morris–Lecar velocity at
#{I_{\mathrm{app}}=100}, and a [center manifold](fnip-0059) tangent
to the center eigenspace when an eigenvalue has real part zero.
[Hodgkin–Huxley](fnip-0063) states the membrane equation, the
Hodgkin–Huxley system, the current–voltage relation, and the
planar reductions.
[Bifurcations and the classes of excitability](fnip-0079) states
the saddle-node, the saddle-node on an invariant circle, the
Andronov–Hopf bifurcation, the classes of excitability, the
Bautin and Bogdanov–Takens points, and the threshold.
The persistence theorem for a slow manifold, the canard account
of that threshold, and the traveling nerve pulse remain absent,
because their sources are absent. The spike as a relaxation
oscillation is not stated. The cost is that those statements
are not in the notes.}

\p{Volume Two, the algorithmic reading named in
[How to read these notes](fnip-0023), is absent. The cost is that a
code, a temporal memory, and a sensorimotor rule have no chapter here.}

\p{The network sentence in [Motivation and aim](fnip-0020), that
ongoing activity is a background process into which a stimulus arrives,
remains a view. The books cited there treat single model neurons.
Deco, Jirsa, and McIntosh (2011) and Arieli, Sterkin, Grinvald, and
Aertsen, Science 273 (1996), are the sources that would let that
sentence stand as evidence, and neither is in hand. The cost is that
the notes make no network claim.}

\p{A result in these notes is a proved statement about a dynamical
system or a calculation in a cited model. A proposal is marked as the
view that carries it. No statement in the notes fixes a biological
mechanism, a parameter value of a living cell, or a clinical claim.}
